Z||000000||anthony_86gt||03-21-2001||07:44 PM||||I need to know which 8" sub hits really good.  I have a jensen 200w amp, and a type 1 box.  im gonna just use one 8. so which 1????  please give me some advice.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||03-21-2001||09:07 PM||||i use a jl audio 8w1 that's worked pretty good for the last couple years. but  if you have another car with a bigger system it will start to seem puny. i've been hoping to make a switch to 3 8w0 12ohm's. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-21-2001||09:38 PM||||I have a Rockford Fostgate XLC 8". It gives excellent bass for its size and specially price. Cost me $60 at Brandsmart in Fl. Also it works good with small enclosure. I have a box no more than 0.7cf. Next week it will go to a smaller box I'm currently fabricating to be in the stock location. Hope it sounds as good there too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||03-21-2001||10:46 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/</A> <P>click on the car products tab on the left. then scroll down to component subs. then scroll down to the mtx section. the first mtx sub listed is the 8" BL84. very good price and the eclosure only needs to be 0.38 cubic foot. i've got a 10" blue thunder mtx that's hits hard and sounds awesome. i'm not sure if this is the exact same model though. but hey, look at the specs. $50 is a really good deal for that nice of a sub.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||10
